  "instructions": [
    "Heat the olive oil in a large clay or ceramic pot over medium heat.",
    "Add the onion, garlic, and ginger, and cook until the onion is translucent.",
    "Add the lamb, cumin, coriander, cinnamon, salt, and pepper, and cook until the lamb is browned.",
    "Add the orange blossom water, apricots, and shio-koji, and bring to a simmer.",
    "Transfer the pot to the oven and cook for 2 hours, or until the lamb is tender and the sauce has thickened.",
    "Stir in the honey and parsley, and season with salt and pepper to taste.",
    "Serve the tagine hot, garnished with chopped parsley and a dollop of yogurt, if desired.",
    "Let the tagine rest for 10 minutes before serving, and serve with couscous or rice.",
    "This recipe makes 6 servings and can be easily doubled or tripled to feed a larger crowd."
